Z||000000||wkayl||08-30-2001||10:07 AM||||What day of the week do you meet?  Weekends seem quite busy around here.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg"> <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||08-30-2001||10:18 AM||||MFF (Minnesota Fieros Forever) meets the 3rd Monday of every month (unless stated otherwise) at a local (Brookdale) Pontiac dealership. Meetings officially start at 7pm and usually only run until 8pm... during the summer months there is usually quite a few people hanging around before and after the meetings just talking.<P>There has been some discussion over location-we've tried at least 5 different places over the last few years and never quite find the right place.  Need a good lot for the cars, a good-sized room for the meeting, and the ability to use it regularily.  Not as easy as it sounds!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-30-2001||12:05 PM||||my car club, not a Fiero one, has its meeting usually the 1st wednesday each month so it dont interfere with weekends/holidays. Once in a while we have them while were at a big cruise in/ show. We have them in a private party room at a big restaurant so no one has a mess to clean up and everyone can eat or drink too.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jaygee79||08-30-2001||12:37 PM||||NEFA only meets once a year so far because we are so widespread (all over New England).  The Board of Directors meets more often though.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Jaime<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR>ICQ: 85931334</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/peggypic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FOCOSEVA||08-30-2001||01:32 PM||||The Fiero Owners Club of Southeast Virginia meets in the mid-afternoon of the third Saturday of each month. A long time ago we took a poll of members, asking what day(s) they would prefer, and it seemed we got as many different answers as there were members, so we arbitrarily chose that day because there wasn't any one day that everybody agreed upon. Also, as for meeting location, since our members are pretty well spread out, we vary the meeting location from one month to the next, to be fair, so that no members always have to drive the farthest distance.<BR>Curry Obenshain <A HREF="http://www.vafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>www.vafieros.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||RDosdorian||08-30-2001||04:37 PM||||Golden Gate Fieros in California meets the third Tuesday of the month.  We have found that weekend dates are good for drives and fun things, but weekdays are better for meetings.<P>Ray Dosdorian<BR>Past President<BR>Golden Gate Fieros<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.goldengatefieros.org/RDosdorian_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||72vinman||08-30-2001||04:41 PM||||I am a new member of The GTA Fiero club here in Toronto. We meet the third Tuesday of every month.<P>------------------<BR>72vinman@home.com<BR>Stock Black 86GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/iannoy/sign.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000007||chester||08-30-2001||04:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaygee79:<BR><B>  The Board of Directors meets more often though.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Really?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  Boy I guess I'm in the wrong place all the time.  I think the statement should be more like "The board of directors SHOULD meet more often"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Rob D.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jaygee79||08-30-2001||05:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by chester:<BR><B> Really?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  Boy I guess I'm in the wrong place all the time.  I think the statement should be more like "The board of directors SHOULD meet more often"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Rob D.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh, they don't?  OK I guess I was wrong LOL<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ranger Jaime<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR>ICQ: 85931334</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/peggypic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||DXR_DAD||08-30-2001||09:10 PM||||Very nice looking GT RDosdorian   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I think a Saturday meeting now and then is good! Day time so we can have some day light and time talk shop and look at the members cars and new mods they have done??<P>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=5080942&p=24416340&Sequence=2&res=high">  <P>What ya think about it Fierobear????? I haven't had a chance to see that 3-4 up close<P><p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||FOCONE||08-30-2001||09:41 PM||||The Fiero Owners Club of New England (FOCONE) does not have meetings like other clubs.  We would like to have meetings but generally the distance we all would have to travel and our personal lives just seems to make it difficult.  So what we do here at FOCONE, is have two Fiero shows a year, Summer and Fall, and that gives most everyone a good fill of Fiero Shows.  The other thing it does is to give those who have more time a chance to diversify by attending other car club events in the area or out of the area.  After all it only comes down to one thing, the Fiero.<P>Chris Schaefer<BR>FOCONE Membership Director/Editor||||reg||10
Z||000011||Ronnie||08-30-2001||10:26 PM||||The Georgia Fieros Club meets the 2nd Saturday of the month at 1:30pm. We always meet at the American Pie restaurant so we can sit down , eat, or just have a cool drink while we discuss our upcoming plans. We try to have someone do a Tech session in the parking lot afterwards such as, headlight rebuild, ignition module replacement, etc.<BR>Usually have a pretty good turnout on Saturdays.<P>------------------<BR>88GT auto,88Formula T-Top,86GT 4spd<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/new_sig_new_paint_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
